---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Terms and Conditions | Tours Peruvian Travel" description="Terms and Conditions for the reservation and provision of tourist services.">
  <div class="pt-24 pb-16 bg-slate-50 min-h-screen">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl shadow-xl p-8 md:p-12 border border-slate-100">
        <div class="mb-6 pb-6 border-b border-slate-100">
          <h1 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-black text-slate-800 mb-2">Terms and Conditions</h1>
          <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm">Last updated: June 2026</p>
        </div>

        <div class="prose prose-slate prose-sm max-w-none prose-headings:font-bold prose-headings:text-slate-800 prose-p:text-slate-600 prose-p:leading-relaxed prose-li:text-slate-600">
          <p>Welcome to <strong>Tours Peruvian service</strong>. By accessing our website or booking any of our services, you agree to be bound by the following terms and conditions. Please read them carefully.</p>
          
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mt-6 mb-3 text-slate-800">1. Bookings and Payments</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5">
            <li>To confirm a reservation, an advance payment is required (percentage specified in each package).</li>
            <li>The remaining balance must be paid before starting the tour, according to the specific conditions of each destination.</li>
            <li>Prices are expressed in Peruvian Soles (PEN) or US Dollars (USD) and include statutory taxes, unless otherwise indicated.</li>
          </ul>
          
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mt-6 mb-3 text-slate-800">2. Cancellation and Refund Policies</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5">
            <li>Cancellations made more than 15 days in advance may be subject to an administrative fee but will allow for a partial refund.</li>
            <li>Cancellations made with less than 7 days' notice are non-refundable, given the operational expenses already incurred for bookings with third parties (hotels, trains, flights).</li>
            <li>In case of a "no show" (failure to appear at the start of the tour), the passenger forfeits 100% of the amount paid.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mt-6 mb-3 text-slate-800">3. Itinerary Modifications</h2>
          <p>The agency reserves the right to modify the tour itinerary due to unforeseen factors such as strikes, roadblocks, adverse weather, or any other force majeure event that puts the integrity of the passengers at risk. Alternatives of similar quality will always be sought.</p>

          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mt-6 mb-3 text-slate-800">4. Passenger Responsibilities</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5">
            <li>It is the passenger's responsibility to carry their valid identity documents (ID, Passport, etc.) at all times.</li>
            <li>The passenger must timely inform us of any dietary restrictions, allergies, or relevant medical conditions before starting the trip.</li>
            <li>Respectful behavior towards staff, other passengers, and the local communities visited is expected.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mt-6 mb-3 text-slate-800">5. Travel Insurance</h2>
          <p>Although our transport services have SOAT (Compulsory Traffic Accident Insurance), we strongly recommend that all passengers purchase comprehensive personal travel insurance covering medical assistance, theft, and unforeseen cancellations.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
